{"id":"mahabharata-8-064","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":64,"title":"चतुःषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 64 · Karna and Arjuna to meet","summary":{"en":"Gods, nagas, siddhas and gandharvas gather to see the two champions fight, and Karna declares he will fight Arjuna alone. Duryodhana urges him on and gives his troops orders to guard the field.","kn":"ಈ ಇಬ್ಬರು ವೀರರ ಹೋರಾಟ ನೋಡಲು ದೇವತೆಗಳು, ನಾಗರು, ಸಿದ್ಧರು, ಗಂಧರ್ವರು ಸೇರುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಕರ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನೊಡನೆ ಒಬ್ಬನೇ ಹೋರಾಡುವೆನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಅವನನ್ನು ಪ್ರೇರಿಸಿ ಸೈನ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ರಣರಂಗ ಕಾಯಲು ಆದೇಶಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दोनों वीरों का युद्ध देखने के लिए देवता, नाग, सिद्ध और गन्धर्व जुटते हैं, और कर्ण कहता है कि वह अर्जुन से अकेला लड़ेगा। दुर्योधन उसे प्रेरित करता है और सेना को रणभूमि की रक्षा का आदेश देता है।","te":"ఈ ఇద్దరు వీరుల పోరు చూడటానికి దేవతలు, నాగులు, సిద్ధులు, గంధర్వులు చేరతారు; అర్జునునితో ఒంటరిగా పోరాడతానని కర్ణుడు అంటాడు. దుర్యోధనుడు అతన్ని ప్రేరేపించి సేనకు రణభూమిని కాపాడమని ఆదేశిస్తాడు.","ta":"இவ்விரு வீரரின் போரைக் காண தேவர், நாகர், சித்தர், கந்தர்வர் கூடுகின்றனர்; அர்ஜுனனுடன் தனியாகப் போரிடுவேன் என்கிறான் கர்ணன். துரியோதனன் அவனைத் தூண்டிப் படைக்குக் களத்தைக் காக்க ஆணையிடுகிறான்.","ml":"രണ്ടു മഹാവീരന്മാർ പൊരുതുന്നത് കാണാൻ ദേവന്മാരും നാഗന്മാരും സിദ്ധന്മാരും ഗന്ധർവന്മാരും ഒന്നിച്ചുകൂടുന്നു; താൻ തനിച്ച് അർജുനനോട് പൊരുതുമെന്ന് കർണ്ണൻ പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു. ദുര്യോധനൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പ്രോത്സാഹിപ്പിക്കുകയും, യുദ്ധക്കളം കാക്കാൻ സൈനികർക്ക് നിർദ്ദേശം നൽകുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.64; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तद्देवनागासुरसिद्धसंघै-\nर्गन्धर्वयक्षाप्सरसां च संघैः ।\nब्रह्मर्षिराजर्षिसुपर्णजुष्टं\nबभौ वियद्विस्मयनीयरूपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sky, thronged with hosts of gods, Nagas, Asuras and Siddhas, with Gandharvas, Yakshas and Apsarases, and visited by Brahmarshis, royal sages and Garudas, shone with a wondrous look."}},{"n":2,"text":"नानद्यमानं निनदैर्मनोज्ञै-\nर्वादित्रगीतस्तुतिभिश्च नृत्तैः ।\nसर्वेऽन्तरिक्षे ददृशुर्मनुष्याः\nखस्थांश्च तान्विस्मयनीयरूपान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It resounded with sweet sounds, with music, songs, hymns and dances; all the men saw those beings in the heavens, wondrous in form."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः प्रहृष्टाः कुरुपाण्डुयोधा\nवादित्रपत्रायुधसिंहनादैः ।\nनिनादयन्तो वसुधां दिशश्च\nस्वनेन सर्वे द्विषतो निजघ्नुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the delighted warriors of the Kurus and Pandavas, with trumpets, banners, weapons and lion-roars, filled the earth and the quarters with sound and struck at their foes with a din."}},{"n":4,"text":"नानाश्वमातङ्गरथायुताकुलं\nवरासिशक्त्यृष्टिनिपातदुःसहम् ।\nअभीरुजुष्टं हतदेहसंकुलं\nरणाजिरं लोहितरक्तमाबभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The battlefield, crowded with many horses, elephants and chariots by the thousand, unbearable for the falling of fine swords, darts and spears, frequented by the fearless and thick with slain bodies, shone red with blood."}},{"n":5,"text":"तथा प्रवृत्तेऽस्त्रभृतां पराभवे\nधनंजयश्चाधिरथिश्च सायकैः ।\nदिशश्च सैन्यं च शितैरजिह्मगैः\nपरस्परं प्रोर्णुवतुः स्म दंशितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the defeat of those who bear weapons went on, Dhananjaya and the son of Adhiratha, both armored, covered the quarters and each other's army with sharp, straight arrows."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततस्त्वदीयाश्च परे च सायकैः\nकृतेऽन्धकारे विविदुर्न किंचन ।\nभयात्तु तावेव रथौ समाश्रयं-\nस्तमोनुदौ खे प्रसृता इवांशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when the arrows made darkness, your men and the enemy could see nothing; in fear they took shelter with those two chariots, which dispelled the gloom like rays spread in the sky."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततोऽस्त्रमस्त्रेण परस्परस्य तौ\nविधूय वाताविव पूर्वपश्चिमौ ।\nघनान्धकारे वितते तमोनुदौ\nयथोदितौ तद्वदतीव रेजतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then each, shaking off the other's missile with his own, like winds from east and west, shone brilliantly in the spreading dense darkness as two dispellers of darkness risen."}},{"n":8,"text":"न चाभिमन्तव्यमिति प्रचोदिताः\nपरे त्वदीयाश्च तदावतस्थिरे ।\nमहारथौ तौ परिवार्य सर्वतः\nसुरासुरा वासवशम्बराविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged on by the thought \"He must not be attacked,\" your men and the others stood still, surrounding those two great chariot-warriors on all sides, as gods and asuras stood around Indra and Shambara."}},{"n":9,"text":"मृदङ्गभेरीपणवानकस्वनै-\nर्निनादिते भारत शङ्खनिस्वनैः ।\nससिंहनादौ बभतुर्नरोत्तमौ\nशशाङ्कसूर्याविव मेघसंप्लवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"O Bharata, with the sound of drums, kettledrums, tabors, gongs and conches, and with lion-roars, those best of men shone like the moon and sun in a flood of clouds."}},{"n":10,"text":"महाधनुर्मण्डलमध्यगावुभौ\nसुवर्चसौ बाणसहस्ररश्मिनौ ।\nदिधक्षमाणौ सचराचरं जग-\nद्युगास्तसूर्याविव दुःसहौ रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both stood in the midst of the great circles of their bows, brilliant, with thousands of arrows for rays, wishing to burn the world of moving and unmoving things, hard to bear in battle like two suns at the end of an age."}},{"n":11,"text":"उभावजेयावहितान्तकावुभौ\nजिघांसतुस्तौ कृतिनौ परस्परम् ।\nमहाहवे वीरवरौ समीयतु-\nर्यथेन्द्रजम्भाविव कर्णपाण्डवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both were unconquerable and the death of their enemies; both skilled, they wished to kill each other; Karna and the Pandava met in the great fight like Indra and Jambha."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो महास्त्राणि महाधनुर्धरौ\nविमुञ्चमानाविषुभिर्भयानकैः ।\nनराश्वनागानमितौ निजघ्नतुः\nपरस्परं जघ्नतुरुत्तमेषुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those two great bowmen, loosing great missiles and fearsome arrows, killed countless men, horses and elephants, and struck each other with their best arrows."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततो विसस्रुः पुनरर्दिताः शरै-\nर्नरोत्तमाभ्यां कुरुपाण्डवाश्रयाः ।\nसनागपत्त्यश्वरथा दिशो गता-\nस्तथा यथा सिंहभयाद्वनौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those who sheltered with the Kurus and Pandavas, tormented again by arrows from the two best of men, fled in all directions with elephants, foot soldiers, horses and chariots, like forest dwellers in fear of a lion."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततस्तु दुर्योधनभोजसौबलाः\nकृपश्च शारद्वतसूनुना सह ।\nमहारथाः पञ्च धनंजयाच्युतौ\nशरैः शरीरान्तकरैरताडयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana, Kritavarman the Bhoja, Shakuni, Kripa and the son of Sharadvat, the five great chariot-warriors, struck Dhananjaya and Achyuta with arrows that end bodies."}},{"n":15,"text":"धनूंषि तेषामिषुधीन्हयान्ध्वजा-\nन्रथांश्च सूतांश्च धनंजयः शरैः ।\nसमं च चिच्छेद पराभिनच्च ता-\nञ्शरोत्तमैर्द्वादशभिश्च सूतजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya cut their bows, quivers, horses, banners, chariots and charioteers with arrows all at once, and pierced them, and with twelve best arrows he pierced Karna."}},{"n":16,"text":"अथाभ्यधावंस्त्वरिताः शतं रथाः\nशतं च नागार्जुनमाततायिनः ।\nशकास्तुखारा यवनाश्च सादिनः\nसहैव काम्बोजवरैर्जिघांसवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a hundred chariots and a hundred elephants rushed at Arjuna, bent on harming him, along with Shakas, Tukharas, Yavanas, horsemen and the best of the Kambojas, wishing to kill him."}},{"n":17,"text":"वरायुधान्पाणिगतान्करैः सह\nक्षुरैर्न्यकृन्तंस्त्वरिताः शिरांसि च ।\nहयांश्च नागांश्च रथांश्च युध्यतां\nधनंजयः शत्रुगणं तमक्षिणोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya swiftly cut with razor arrows the fine weapons in their hands, along with the hands, and their heads, and wore down that host of enemies, the horses, elephants and chariots of the fighters."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततोऽन्तरिक्षे सुरतूर्यनिस्वनाः\nससाधुवादा हृषितैः समीरिताः ।\nनिपेतुरप्युत्तमपुष्पवृष्टयः\nसुरूपगन्धाः पवनेरिताः शिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the sky there sounded divine trumpets and cries of approval raised by the delighted, and the best showers of flowers fell, auspicious and fair in fragrance, driven by the wind."}},{"n":19,"text":"तदद्भुतं देवमनुष्यसाक्षिकं\nसमीक्ष्य भूतानि विसिष्मियुर्नृप ।\nतवात्मजः सूतसुतश्च न व्यथां\nन विस्मयं जग्मतुरेकनिश्चयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that wonder with gods and men as witnesses, the beings were amazed, O king; but your son and the charioteer's son, of one purpose, felt neither pain nor wonder."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथाब्रवीद्द्रोणसुतस्तवात्मजं\nकरं करेण प्रतिपीड्य सान्त्वयन् ।\nप्रसीद दुर्योधन शाम्य पाण्डवै-\nरलं विरोधेन धिगस्तु विग्रहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son pressed your son's hand with his and said to him in comfort: \"Be calm, Duryodhana, make peace with the Pandavas; enough of enmity, shame on war."}},{"n":21,"text":"हतो गुरुर्ब्रह्मसमो महास्त्रवि-\nत्तथैव भीष्मप्रमुखा नरर्षभाः ।\nअहं त्ववध्यो मम चापि मातुलः\nप्रशाधि राज्यं सह पाण्डवैश्चिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our guru, equal to Brahma and master of great missiles, is slain, and so are Bhishma and the other bulls among men. I am not to be killed and neither is my maternal uncle; rule the kingdom a long while with the Pandavas."}},{"n":22,"text":"धनंजयः स्थास्यति वारितो मया\nजनार्दनो नैव विरोधमिच्छति ।\nयुधिष्ठिरो भूतहिते सदा रतो\nवृकोदरस्तद्वशगस्तथा यमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya will stay if I restrain him; Janardana wants no enmity at all; Yudhishthira is always devoted to the good of beings, and Vrikodara and the twins follow his lead."}},{"n":23,"text":"त्वया च पार्थैश्च परस्परेण\nप्रजाः शिवं प्राप्नुयुरिच्छति त्वयि ।\nव्रजन्तु शेषाः स्वपुराणि पार्थिवा\nनिवृत्तवैराश्च भवन्तु सैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With peace between you and the Parthas, the people will find well-being, if you wish it; let the remaining kings go to their own cities and the soldiers lay down their enmity."}},{"n":24,"text":"न चेद्वचः श्रोष्यसि मे नराधिप\nध्रुवं प्रतप्तासि हतोऽरिभिर्युधि ।\nइदं च दृष्टं जगता सह त्वया\nकृतं यदेकेन किरीटमालिना ।\nयथा न कुर्याद्बलभिन्न चान्तको\nन च प्रचेता भगवान्न यक्षराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you will not listen to me, O lord of men, you will surely be tormented, slain by your enemies in battle. You have also seen with the world what the garlanded diadem-wearer alone has done: neither Indra, nor Death, nor lord Varuna, nor the king of Yakshas could do it."}},{"n":25,"text":"अतोऽपि भूयांश्च गुणैर्धनंजयः\nस चाभिपत्स्यत्यखिलं वचो मम ।\nतवानुयात्रां च तथा करिष्यति\nप्रसीद राजञ्जगतः शमाय वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya is even greater in his qualities, and he will accept all my words and will follow you in your journey. Be gracious, O king, for the peace of the world."}},{"n":26,"text":"ममापि मानः परमः सदा त्वयि\nब्रवीम्यतस्त्वां परमाच्च सौहृदात् ।\nनिवारयिष्यामि हि कर्णमप्यहं\nयदा भवान्सप्रणयो भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"My regard for you is always the highest, and I speak to you from the deepest friendship; I will restrain even Karna once you are well disposed.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"वदन्ति मित्रं सहजं विचक्षणा-\nस्तथैव साम्ना च धनेन चार्जितम् ।\nप्रतापतश्चोपनतं चतुर्विधं\nतदस्ति सर्वं त्वयि पाण्डवेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise speak of four kinds of friend: the natural, the one won by conciliation, the one won by wealth and the one come by force; all of that exists between you and the Pandavas."}},{"n":28,"text":"निसर्गतस्ते तव वीर बान्धवाः\nपुनश्च साम्ना च समाप्नुहि स्थिरम् ।\nत्वयि प्रसन्ने यदि मित्रतामियु-\nर्ध्रुवं नरेन्द्रेन्द्र तथा त्वमाचर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They are your kin by nature, hero; win them by conciliation and keep them firmly. If, when you are pleased, they turn to friendship, then act so, lord of kings.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"स एवमुक्तः सुहृदा वचो हितं\nविचिन्त्य निःश्वस्य च दुर्मनाब्रवीत् ।\nयथा भवानाह सखे तथैव त-\nन्ममापि च ज्ञापयतो वचः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by his friend with good advice, Duryodhana thought, sighed, and said gloomily: \"It is as you say, friend; but hear my words, who also tell you the truth."}},{"n":30,"text":"निहत्य दुःशासनमुक्तवान्बहु\nप्रसह्य शार्दूलवदेष दुर्मतिः ।\nवृकोदरस्तद्धृदये मम स्थितं\nन तत्परोक्षं भवतः कुतः शमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That wicked Vrikodara, after killing Duhshasana, spoke much, forcibly, like a tiger; that stays in my heart and is not hidden from you; how can there be peace?"}},{"n":31,"text":"न चापि कर्णं गुरुपुत्र संस्तवा-\nदुपारमेत्यर्हसि वक्तुमच्युत ।\nश्रमेण युक्तो महताद्य फल्गुन-\nस्तमेष कर्णः प्रसभं हनिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor, son of the guru, should you, out of friendship, tell Karna to stop, Achyuta. Phalguna today is exhausted with great toil, and Karna will forcibly kill him.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"तमेवमुक्त्वाभ्यनुनीय चासकृ-\nत्तवात्मजः स्वाननुशास्ति सैनिकान् ।\nसमाघ्नताभिद्रवताहितानिमा-\nन्सबाणशब्दान्किमु जोषमास्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thus spoken to him and soothed him repeatedly, your son ordered his own soldiers: \"Strike, rush upon these enemies amid the sound of arrows; why do you sit silent?\""}}]}]}